# Debug

## Core

- Reproduce (or gather equivalent evidence) before changing code. Don't guess with many unrelated edits.
- Prefer runtime proof: logs, stack traces, failing tests, bisect, bisected commits — over guesses.
- Screenshot / live-UI bugs: capture the live page (snapshot and/or screenshot) when available; don't guess from description alone.
- Find the root cause, then apply the smallest correct fix. Don't hide the bug with retries or catch-alls unless that is the real fix.
- Stay in scope: fix the bug you were asked to fix; park unrelated issues as follow-ups.
- Say what is known, what changed the diagnosis, and what remains uncertain. If you can't repro, say so and stop guessing.
